Replay harness patch: one trusted-input primitive, no rule changes (XXII.B)
=========================================================================

The exported objects contain IMPORT leaves: sequents that existed in the
recording environment before recording began.  They are name-free by design,
so a fresh session cannot look them up, and fusion.ml exposes no way to admit
a sequent with hypotheses without *changing the axiom registry* (new_axiom only
admits a closed statement; mk_thm in drule.ml is itself built on new_axiom).

This patch adds three functions to the kernel signature:

    val proof_import : term list * term -> thm
    val proof_const  : string * hol_type -> term
    val proof_type   : string * hol_type list -> hol_type

`proof_import` packages an already-recorded sequent as a theorem with axiom
mask 0 and node id -1.  It checks only that every term is boolean.

`proof_const` and `proof_type` are raw constructors: they rebuild the
object's own constant and type-operator occurrences exactly as recorded,
without adding anything to the session signature.  The object is
self-contained (every term carries its full type), and constants the prelude
declared (e.g. s2n-bignum's `:=`) must not be re-declared monomorphically in a
fresh session.

None of the three is an inference rule, none is used by any recorded node, and
none touches the axioms or the definition registry.  They are the explicit
boundary at which the replay accepts the same object-side signature and the
same imported premises the Rust checker reads from its `.hlst` store.  Every
node with rule != IMPORT is rebuilt with the stock primitives.

Apply to a *copy* of `.bench/hol-light-objects`; never to the recording kernel.

--- a/fusion.ml
+++ b/fusion.ml
@@ -101,4 +101,10 @@
       val proof_record_begin : unit -> unit
       val proof_node_count : unit -> int
       val proof_export : string -> thm -> unit
+
+      (* Trusted input for the replay harness.  Admits the recording
+         environment's sequents and rebuilds its signature; not inferences. *)
+      val proof_import : term list * term -> thm
+      val proof_const : string * hol_type -> term
+      val proof_type : string * hol_type list -> hol_type
 end;;
@@ -947,4 +953,13 @@
 
   let axioms() = !the_axioms
 
+  let proof_import (asl,c) =
+    if List.for_all (fun t -> compare (type_of t) bool_ty = 0) (c::asl)
+    then Sequent((asl,c),0,(-1))
+    else failwith "proof_import: hypotheses and conclusion must be boolean"
+
+  let proof_const (n,ty) = Const(n,ty)
+
+  let proof_type (n,args) = Tyapp(n,args)
+
   let new_axiom tm =
